$NetBSD$

Pass --force to makeinfo, as the other three doc directories of this same
release already do.

23.4 ships four texinfo makefiles.  doc/emacs, doc/lispref and doc/misc all
say "MAKEINFO = makeinfo --force"; doc/lispintro alone says just "makeinfo".
The manual it builds has not been valid texinfo for a long time --

	emacs-lisp-intro.texi:4626: @itemx must follow @item

-- and a makeinfo strict enough to call that an error rather than a warning
stops the whole bootstrap there:

	gmake[3]: *** [Makefile:49: ../../info/eintr] Error 1

texinfo 7.2 is strict enough.  With --force the same run produces
../../info/eintr and exits 0, with the remaining complaints as warnings.

Upstream did not fix the asymmetry; it went away in 24.1, where all four
makefiles take MAKEINFO from configure instead of spelling it out.

--- doc/lispintro/Makefile.in.orig
+++ doc/lispintro/Makefile.in
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 INFO_TARGETS = ${infodir}/eintr
 DVI_TARGETS = emacs-lisp-intro.dvi
 
-MAKEINFO = makeinfo
+MAKEINFO = makeinfo --force
 TEXI2DVI = texi2dvi
 TEXI2PDF = texi2pdf
 DVIPS = dvips
